   "advances_plan": "Parnesse protects herself and your permanents with a 4-life targeting tax, and her copy-sharing is a political tool.",
   "honest_note": "None of the 25 Spellbook infinites in the list uses Parnesse; all are copy-spell pairs that work in any Grixis spellslinger deck. Her second ability gives opponents copies, which is optional politics and can be a liability. The source frames the deck as political conversion (blueprint L12), but mechanically she's a five-mana protection/politics commander on top of a strong generic copy-combo shell. The calibration floor is 3, below the source's 4; the 25 two-card infinites support 4. M1 review (parnesse-01..10) flags Bonus Round as symmetric (parnesse-07) and leaves one question uncertain (parnesse-10: whether opponents' retargeted copies pay her 4-life tax)."
